<!--
  Ship UI landing — the front door. Umbrella across the four products, so it must
  say what each one IS in a sentence, not describe compilers.

  It was stale: it linked to a tutorial that no longer exists, claimed "around 74
  primitives" (it is 48), and opened with "A compiler-first component framework,
  an app framework, a batteries-included component library, and agent tooling" —
  four nouns and no idea.
-->
<column class="landing-wrap">
  <column class="hero" gap="4">
    <p class="eyebrow">SHIP UI · 0.2.0</p>
    <h1>Everything you need to build a web app.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A component library, a design system, a framework, and the app layer around
      it — so a page is markup, and nothing has to be assembled first.
    </p>
    <row class="hero-cta" gap="2">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/overview">Get started</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/components">See the components</a>
    </row>
  </column>

  <center sx="py:8 px:4">
    <card sx="p:5 max-w:panel-max-w-md" motion:hover={{ scale: 'spring:gentle' }}>
      <column gap="3">
        <row gap="3" align="center">
          <avatar></avatar>
          <column gap="1">
            <strong>Ada Lovelace</strong>
            <p sx="fg:muted-foreground text:sm">Engineering</p>
          </column>
          <badge tone="success">Active</badge>
        </row>
        <row gap="2">
          <button variant="solid" tone="primary" motion:press={{ scale: 'press' }}>Invite</button>
          <button variant="ghost">Export</button>
        </row>
      </column>
    </card>
  </center>
  <center>
    <p sx="text:sm fg:muted-foreground">
      That is real, and it is running. Change the theme in the top right.
    </p>
  </center>

  <column class="products" gap="3">
    <a class="product-card" href="/overview">
      <h3>SUI <small class="tag">framework</small></h3>
      <p>Components, layout, styling, theming, animation and state. Write a page in markup; the framework already has the rest.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/components">
      <h3>Components <small class="tag">48, included</small></h3>
      <p>Buttons, dialogs, combobox, tabs, tables, toasts — accessible, keyboard-complete, and themed. Nothing to install.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/deck">
      <h3>Deck <small class="tag">app framework</small></h3>
      <p>Routing, server rendering, bundling, live data, and a hot-reloading dev loop. The application layer.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/ai">
      <h3>AI <small class="tag">agent tooling</small></h3>
      <p>Built to be written by agents: the compiler is the guardrail, plus MCP tooling and a scored authoring eval.</p>
    </a>
  </column>
</column>
